savers behind them absorb the default risk which flips the usual semiconductor financing model on its head.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:27.500
Trim any single name semiconductor sleeve above 5% of the portfolio until volume confirmation

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:33.600
returns above the 20-day average. Lundin Gold reported strong earnings, a dividend hike,

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:39.020
and steady production guidance, a mix that gives income-oriented investors a reason to revisit

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:45.880
the name against a precious metals cap. Review lug.to position size against that allocation limit

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:50.980
before adding on the news, because a higher payout does not automatically mean the slot in the

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:59.300
portfolio got bigger. Across the simulated book we have 50 trades at a 56% win rate, 28 wins for

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:09.920
a cumulative profit of $333.39 on $1,000 per ticket. Average return per trade is plus 0.67%,

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:18.040
the best trade plus 20.11%, the worst minus 11.80%, and the current streak is one win.

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:25.300
The matched window alpha versus the NASDAQ stands at minus 1.9% across 10 verified window traders,

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:30.280
so we are still behind the benchmark that matters, and that is a challenge, not a crisis.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:36.500
The models are adjusting towards sector rotation checks before catalyst entries, which is the pattern

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:41.540
the recent film sessions keep repeating. Here is something most retail investors get wrong,

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:47.700
and it cost me a clean rebalance before I learn to ignore the pretty pie chart. Imagine you opened

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:55.560
your TFSAO on July 1st with a 60-40 equity bond target after a strong June reset. By September 30th,

00:10:55.760 --> 00:11:02.520
the equity sleeve is sitting at 68%, because one holding ran up 25%, and the brokerage screen

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:08.760
still draws the original 60-40 slices as if nothing happened. That is drift. Time-weighted

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:14.300
returns compound the overweight automatically, so the real allocation walks away from target without

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:20.220
a single new deposit or withdrawal. Professionals pull the full transaction history and calculate both

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:25.260
time-weighted return, which judges the quality of the holdings and money-weighted return,

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:31.440
which judges your personal timing before they touch a rebalance ticket. The move most people skip

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:38.380
is exporting the realized gain report first. That one CSV tells you exactly how much room remains in

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:43.780
the 0% capital gains bracket for the rest of a low-income year, which is the number that should

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:50.000
decided whether you trim inside the TFSA now or wait. The misconception is treating the brokerage

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:56.640
target allocation pie as gospel. It ignores dollar drift and tax lot detail, and those two things are

00:11:56.640 --> 00:12:03.700
the actual trade. Your homework. Open the brokerage app, pull the last 90 days of realized gain transactions

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:10.920
for the TFSA, and write down the dollar amount still available in that 0% long-term capital gains bracket

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:17.120
before your end. If the AI agent side of this valuation work is the part you want to go deeper on,

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:23.260
models and agents covers that beat daily. Before we wrap, tomorrow I will be watching whether

